<!--
  Hub studio · `/studio/components/:name` — the single-component viewer.

  Composes the `@ship/studio` pack's <ship-component-viewer>, passing
  the route's `[name]` param as the viewer's `tag` prop. The composite
  owns the BACKEND-GAP data story (no `ship.ui.components.detail` op +
  the shell's purged catalog endpoint + the framework-stopped catalog
  write) and renders the documented empty-state for every tag today.
  The route is a thin composition — chrome is the root layout, the
  page body is the pack component + the `tag` prop binding.

  Top chrome: the <ship-nav-top> is owned by the root layout
  (`routes/_layout.sui` → `<ship-app-chrome>`). The breadcrumb trail
  auto-derives from `location.pathname` and shows
  `/studio/components/:name`.

  Per the hub-buildout-charter §Connect-only, the viewer needs a
  `ship.ui.components.detail({ tag })` op that does not exist today.
  The component's `entry` derived is the stable boundary — when the
  backend ships the op, the controller's `entry` becomes a
  `live(() => ship.ui.components.detail({ tag: tag() }))` and the
  template's `state() === 'found'` branch renders props / slots /
  source / snippet without a template change.
-->
  <ship-component-viewer prop:tag={name()}></ship-component-viewer>
</main>
